2026-05-12 21:22:53,778 subagents.b_hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[important] persistence[3].columns[1] — "points_per_dollar": role is set to "ratio", but the spec defines ratio exclusively as a fractional value bounded between 0 and 1. A points-per-dollar earn rate (e.g. 10 points per dollar spent) is a whole-number multiplier that routinely exceeds 1. The same incorrect kind propagates into externalContracts[5].responseShape and externalContracts[6].requestShape/responseShape. The LLD will select a fractional 0–1 storage type and may silently clamp or reject any configured value above 1.
2026-05-12 21:22:53,778 subagents.b_hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[important] capabilities[6] — "record-redemption" declares usesWorkflow: true, but per spec usesWorkflow must be false on initial-state inserts — it applies only to capabilities that own subsequent status transitions. record-redemption inserts a redemption row at a fixed initial status and never transitions it; cancel-redemption owns the transition. Marking it true will cause the LLD to generate transition-handling scaffolding (guard checks, allowed-transition logic) for a plain insert operation.
2026-05-12 21:22:53,778 subagents.b_hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[important] edgeCases[5] — The edge case states "a reconciliation note must exist in the redemption record" for abandoned-cart redemptions, but the point_redemptions table has no column of role text or flag to store such a note, and there is no schedule trigger or capability declared to detect or flag stale active redemptions. The LLD has no backing persistence column or job to implement this requirement — it is an orphan promise that cannot be built from the current plan.
